I enter the museum's small cafe.
I go near the counter and buy one 'cutting chai'.
I take the tea and sit near the window.
Outside in the courtyard, there is heavy rain again.
This rain is very beautiful.
Five months ago, the weather was completely dry.
But now there is water everywhere.
A woman sits at the table near me.
She also looks outside.
She looks at me and says, "It is raining heavily today, isn't it?"
I smile and say, "Yes, this rain is very heavy."
The woman asks, "Are you new in Mumbai?"
"Yes, I came here just five months ago," I say.
She laughs and says, "That is great."
"Then this is your first monsoon," she says.
I nod my head and drink the tea.
That tea is very hot.
In this cold weather, hot tea is always good.
